WEBVTT

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.380
You've quite the appetite, miss!

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:17.040
I like that!

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:21.990
Visibly showing your enjoyment of good food displays appreciation to the chef, no?

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.390
You got that right.

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:26.770
Is that how it works?

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:29.510
Oh, there you are!

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:33.030
Regarding the waterwheel you fixed last week...

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:36.650
I talked to the village elder, 
and he was very pleased.

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:37.720
See?

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:40.590
Helping others isn't so bad, is it?

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:41.740
I guess not.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:45.840
And for that, we've added a little bonus to your pay.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:47.540
Thanks!

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:52.590
First, the flour's worth 18 sen a bag,

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:54.840
so 20 bags is 360 sen.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:56.300
And...

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:59.430
1,500 sen for fixing the waterwheel.

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:02.700
Since you ground an additional 
10 bags with the waterwheel,

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:04.940
the total comes to...

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:08.310
Um, about 1,800 sen?

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:09.850
2,040 sen, right?

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:12.750
You can't just say whatever number you want.

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:15.070
You're right. It's 2,040 sen.

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:17.900
Oh, uh, yeah!

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:20.480
I ended up with pretty much the same number!

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:23.610
Here. Thanks for your help.

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:03.800
1,866 times 17.

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:06.190
31,722.

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:10.390
61,488 divided by 24.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:11.810
2,562.

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:14.400
That's right...

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.020
You got them all correct.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:18.140
Is it really that surprising?

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:20.530
Those calculations aren't especially hard.

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:21.880
I see...

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:24.320
I guess this is what you're good at, after all.

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:25.700
"This"?

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.580
As a job!

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:30.790
That again?

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:31.770
Yeah.

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:33.640
Not much work around here needs math,

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:36.310
but there should be plenty of opportunities in the capital.

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:37.290
The capital?

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:38.180
Did you hear?

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:39.930
There was another gigiri attack.

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:42.840
I heard the guys who went to the 
fields this morning were attacked.

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:48.830
Oh, Kuon-san.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.260
Good timing.

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:55.520
Ow! I'm gonna die!

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:57.860
It's just a gigiri bite. Stop wailing so much.

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:01.350
I'm done for!

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:02.860
Hang in there, okay?

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:10.600
Stay still.

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:16.320
<i>Poor guy.</i>

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:18.600
<i>That salve stings like hell!</i>

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:28.280
Don't worry.

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:30.140
This salve doesn't sting.

00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:31.560
<i>You little!</i>

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:33.720
Stay put for a while.

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:35.970
The pain will subside soon.

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:47.600
From what I see, manual labor isn't appropriate for you...

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:46.750
Hey, you two.

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:47.980
Back already?

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:49.350
Good timing.

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:50.080
Oh,

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:52.430
you're leaving already?

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:57.080
Nah, the elder here asked me 
to take care of some gigiri,

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:59.340
so I've got a proposal for you.

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:01.220
Want to come along?

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:02.220
Me?

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:04.090
I saw you treat that guy back there.

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:06.640
You ain't half bad.

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:10.230
An herbalist would be handy to have in a pinch.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:12.540
I'll pay you well.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:20.620
Sure, but on one condition.

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:22.150
Haku comes along too.

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:35.300
You've got quite a big group, don't you?

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:38.500
Honestly, gigiri don't require 
this kind of manpower.

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:41.460
But it's a good chance for them to get practice.

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:45.520
Hey, you okay, man?

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:49.500
No. I'm going to die.

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:50.480
I'm done for!

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:53.530
We haven't even been in the 
mountains for half an hour.

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:54.940
I'm finished.

00:05:54.940 --> 00:05:57.020
I can't take another step.

00:05:57.420 --> 00:06:01.590
Sheesh. Why'd we bring a weakling like him along?

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:03.500
Oh, fine.

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:06.280
Ride on that for a while and rest.

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:08.190
Thanks.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:11.820
I'm saved...

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:21.740
Don't mind him.

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:24.790
This guy's the brains of our little bunch.

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:28.260
His name's Maroro. He's a court scholar.

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:30.050
The brains of the bunch?

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:31.270
Him?

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:37.480
I <i>told</i> you to walk!

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:40.650
If the cart makes you sick you should have walked.{Riding in a cart when you're prone to motion sickness really wasn't the brightest idea.}{too long}

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:42.980
It is improper for a man of noble rank,

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:45.460
such as myself, to trudge up a mountain!

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:47.250
Fine, fine.

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:50.070
Noble, huh?

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:54.650
Hey, your name's Maroro, right?

00:06:55.980 --> 00:06:58.270
I've been wondering something...

00:06:58.270 --> 00:06:59.790
What's a gigiri?

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:02.580
You don't know what a gigiri is?

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:04.460
Nope. No clue.

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:06.590
A gigiri is an insect.

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:10.820
They're long and slender,

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:12.910
with lots of legs.

00:07:13.690 --> 00:07:16.190
Their bodies are covered by hard carapaces,

00:07:16.190 --> 00:07:18.520
and they have great jaws like a pair of scissors...

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:20.460
Wait a second!

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:22.940
You're going to fight a monster like that!?

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:23.810
Hm?

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:25.700
I mean, if it's so huge—

00:07:28.290 --> 00:07:30.110
Here it comes!

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:33.710
Wait, hold it in!

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:35.190
You're a noble, aren't you?

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:38.960
Ukon!

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:40.840
Get over here!

00:07:50.010 --> 00:07:51.430
It stinks!

00:07:51.430 --> 00:07:52.710
What the heck is that?

00:07:52.710 --> 00:07:53.730
Oh, that?

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:55.730
It's a stew of rotten meat.

00:07:55.730 --> 00:07:57.380
Gigiri love it.

00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:00.550
<i>Gigiri, huh?</i>

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:05.140
<i>I wasn't exactly planning on crossing paths again.</i>

00:08:06.310 --> 00:08:07.560
Really, though...

00:08:08.290 --> 00:08:11.570
Will a net that thin be able to hold it?{it would look better is we could split this sentecen}

00:08:28.870 --> 00:08:30.300
Those are pretty big.

00:08:30.890 --> 00:08:33.320
<i>Big? Those?</i>

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:34.210
Maroro.

00:08:34.210 --> 00:08:36.830
I-If I must.

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:40.170
Ahem.

00:08:40.170 --> 00:08:43.030
ompokoko un kurakura

00:08:43.030 --> 00:08:44.690
potanum pasalang

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:46.700
saen shaksam poto ya

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:47.850
hooi sasa

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:50.520
What... is he doing?

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:52.120
Thaumaturgy.

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:54.360
I guess they call it "magic" around here.

00:09:06.680 --> 00:09:09.380
You guys take care of the rest!

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:11.100
Come, men!

00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:31.720
Here, drink up.

00:09:31.720 --> 00:09:33.270
Th-Thanks.

00:09:33.770 --> 00:09:36.470
You've never done something like this before?

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:38.740
Yeah, I guess not.

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:41.320
I really appreciate it.

00:09:41.740 --> 00:09:42.030
Than—

00:10:37.810 --> 00:10:39.340
Haku, catch!

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:42.220
Take this!

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:44.600
Men, we're retreating!

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:46.470
Haku!

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:47.970
R-Right!

00:10:50.450 --> 00:10:52.100
M-My legs...

00:10:53.010 --> 00:10:57.230
They're shaking so much I can't stand...

00:10:57.980 --> 00:11:00.120
Don't leave me here!

00:11:01.870 --> 00:11:03.870
Haku, hurry!

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:23.820
You still in one piece, kid?

00:11:24.340 --> 00:11:25.610
Yeah, somehow.

00:11:25.610 --> 00:11:28.640
And Maroro... is okay too, I guess.

00:11:29.090 --> 00:11:31.300
That was something else, kid.

00:11:31.930 --> 00:11:34.030
You saved his life.

00:11:34.030 --> 00:11:36.350
Just so we're clear,
I'm not carrying anyone next time!

00:11:36.350 --> 00:11:37.750
Never, ever!

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:40.830
I owe you my thanks too, miss.

00:11:40.830 --> 00:11:42.260
Don't worry about it.

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:44.530
I'll be sending you the bill later.

00:11:44.530 --> 00:11:46.580
Yeah, look forward to it!

00:11:47.170 --> 00:11:49.930
I wasn't expecting a boro-gigiri, though.

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:51.200
Oh right, Kuon.

00:11:51.550 --> 00:11:52.040
Here.

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:56.740
You hang on to that.

00:11:56.740 --> 00:11:58.210
It's like a good luck charm.

00:11:58.710 --> 00:11:59.870
Yeah?

00:12:00.420 --> 00:12:02.300
Well then, thanks.

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:05.940
That big one is following us.

00:12:06.610 --> 00:12:07.930
So it seems.

00:12:10.190 --> 00:12:12.690
If that thing reaches the village, it'll be a bloodbath.

00:12:13.530 --> 00:12:15.590
We need to kill it here.

00:12:15.590 --> 00:12:18.190
Right. I'll rally everyone who can still move.

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:22.940
No, you guys take the 
wounded back to the village.

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:25.690
But... we can still fight!

00:12:25.690 --> 00:12:27.640
Get them back safely.

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:29.910
What, are you worried about me?

00:12:32.090 --> 00:12:33.320
All right.

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:39.960
Okay, see you around.

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:42.960
Where do you think you're going, Haku?

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:45.950
By the way, Ukon.

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:47.440
What was that big thing?

00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:50.720
Oh, that's no normal gigiri.

00:12:50.720 --> 00:12:52.090
It's a boro-gigiri.

00:12:52.090 --> 00:12:54.330
I'd never seen one before, either.

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:55.980
Wh-When the gigiri...

00:12:55.980 --> 00:12:57.980
Oh, you're awake?

00:12:58.290 --> 00:13:01.230
When the gigiri enter their
breeding season,

00:13:01.230 --> 00:13:04.360
some of them grow extremely large and bear children.

00:13:04.360 --> 00:13:06.490
That's what we call a boro-gigiri.

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:09.230
Wow, I guess you really are a scholar.

00:13:09.230 --> 00:13:10.750
You sure know a lot.

00:13:10.750 --> 00:13:14.930
But I have no idea how to 
kill a monster that size.

00:13:16.910 --> 00:13:19.940
A boro-gigiri, huh?

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:22.000
Haku?

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:24.580
Hey, Kuon,

00:13:24.580 --> 00:13:28.310
where was it that you found me again?

00:13:28.310 --> 00:13:29.590
Huh?

00:13:29.590 --> 00:13:32.970
Well, it was over there.

00:13:32.970 --> 00:13:35.390
Don't you remember the shape of that ridge?

00:13:36.410 --> 00:13:37.530
Right.

00:13:38.140 --> 00:13:41.020
That means it should still be there.

00:13:41.770 --> 00:13:43.330
"It"?

00:13:44.570 --> 00:13:46.300
You mean the curse?

00:13:47.030 --> 00:13:50.890
If we can bring that thing there somehow...

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:52.850
Oh, I get it!

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:55.030
That's a great idea!

00:13:55.730 --> 00:13:57.210
No, hang on.

00:13:57.210 --> 00:13:58.960
I was just throwing out ideas.

00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:00.860
No, it'll work!

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:03.460
Looks like I was right to bring you along!

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:05.590
Hey, you can't just decide that!

00:14:05.590 --> 00:14:08.220
How would we even get to 
that mountain right now?

00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:11.430
Hey, don't leave me hanging, you two.

00:14:08.940 --> 00:14:11.430
Okay, give me a second.

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:15.720
Hey, Kuon!

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:17.980
If anything happens, use this!

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:24.610
Take care of the rest!

00:14:25.580 --> 00:14:27.840
Take care of it how?

00:14:28.410 --> 00:14:30.510
What's going on, kid?

00:14:31.110 --> 00:14:34.330
I'll say up front that I 
don't know if this will work.

00:14:34.790 --> 00:14:36.870
Don't blame me if it fails.

00:14:51.010 --> 00:14:54.930
<i>I was attacked by a boro-gigiri 
once before and survived.</i>

00:14:55.400 --> 00:14:58.470
<i>So all we have to do is recreate that situation.</i>

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:01.070
<i>There's a curse in these snowy mountains.</i>

00:15:01.070 --> 00:15:03.810
<i>We'll draw it out into the path of the boro-gigiri.</i>

00:15:16.150 --> 00:15:17.420
The little ones are coming!

00:15:17.420 --> 00:15:17.990
Move it!

00:16:01.610 --> 00:16:04.950
Hey, come on... This is crazy.

00:16:12.090 --> 00:16:13.840
Victory!{Hiyahhoyu}

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:16.130
That's our Master Ukon!{After looking up -dono a bit, I found out that it's often used by someone with higher rank addressing the lower rank. I think Maroro with his "noble" character fit this definition of -dono usage better}

00:16:16.130 --> 00:16:16.950
Don't get careless!

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:18.570
We're not done yet! Get back!

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:42.190
Ukon!

00:16:42.190 --> 00:16:43.450
Master Ukon!

00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:46.460
Relax, this is nothing.

00:16:50.390 --> 00:16:53.460
Now, what to do?

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:56.190
Okay, it's time.

00:16:56.190 --> 00:16:57.970
Both of you, close your eyes!

00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:29.040
Great work, kid!

00:17:29.810 --> 00:17:32.040
Haku! Haku!

00:17:32.620 --> 00:17:34.330
Haku!

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:40.290
You're late, miss.

00:17:40.290 --> 00:17:44.040
Wh-What good is it from all the way down <i>there</i>!?

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:44.680
Ukon!

00:17:44.920 --> 00:17:47.690
Could you repeat that attack of yours?

00:17:47.690 --> 00:17:53.190
Sure, but she's just going to dodge it again.

00:17:53.560 --> 00:17:55.350
You won't be aiming for her.

00:17:55.910 --> 00:17:56.690
Aim there.

00:17:58.210 --> 00:17:59.450
You mean...

00:17:59.450 --> 00:18:01.060
Don't screw it up.

00:18:01.060 --> 00:18:02.330
Seriously, don't.

00:18:02.330 --> 00:18:04.680
You're breaking my heart here, kid.

00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:06.480
I'm in!

00:18:35.930 --> 00:18:37.400
Did you miss me?

00:18:37.990 --> 00:18:39.070
You're a lifesaver!

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:22.830
You've had your fill, haven't you?

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:25.220
Just go home.

00:19:52.070 --> 00:19:53.620
We're saved!

00:19:56.660 --> 00:20:00.440
You're one hell of an interesting guy.

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:04.490
Yeah, you were right to bring him along.

00:20:06.450 --> 00:20:08.650
Thanks.

00:20:09.870 --> 00:20:12.580
Eat up! The villagers are offering 
this feast to show their thanks.

00:20:13.120 --> 00:20:15.310
You can drink all you'd like tonight!

00:20:21.710 --> 00:20:22.970
Help us out again sometime.

00:20:28.650 --> 00:20:30.970
I think I had too much to drink.

00:20:44.850 --> 00:20:46.570
Beautiful moon, isn't it?{"The moon is beautiful" means "I love you" in Japanese}

00:20:48.510 --> 00:20:50.370
Come with me for a bit.{tsukiau can also mean "go out with me". Haku x Ukon}

00:20:58.870 --> 00:20:59.810
What's this?

00:21:01.030 --> 00:21:02.920
I'm late...

00:21:03.300 --> 00:21:05.760
Guess I'm the last one to do it.

00:21:06.790 --> 00:21:09.830
Dwelling on unpleasantries isn't really our thing.

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:14.130
Whenever we send someone off,
the rule is that we do it with a smile.

00:21:14.130 --> 00:21:15.330
I see.

00:21:18.020 --> 00:21:21.200
We have seen your life 
in this world to its end.

00:21:21.200 --> 00:21:23.530
For now, rest in peace.

00:21:25.440 --> 00:21:29.920
And someday, we shall drink 
again together at Kotoahamuru.

00:21:34.570 --> 00:21:35.290
Now, then...

00:21:35.900 --> 00:21:37.290
Shall we head back and drink more?

00:21:37.970 --> 00:21:39.790
Yeah, sounds good.

00:21:44.500 --> 00:21:45.300
Thanks.

00:21:46.720 --> 00:21:49.050
The water was good.
